Ze-Reviewed-Against: github.com/vishvananda/netlink v1.3.1

parseXfrmState refuses a message shorter than struct xfrm_usersa_info
before it reads the header. Upstream hands the buffer to
nl.DeserializeXfrmUsersaInfo, which slices it to SizeofXfrmUsersaInfo with
no length check, so a truncated reply either panics or is decoded from
bytes past its end. TestZeXfrmStateParserRejectsTruncatedHeader calls the
parser for every short length, the empty reply included. The test file
still carries a Ze design header and a name from Ze's state scope work, so
it is not yet in the form an upstream pull request would carry.

No upstream pull request is opened yet for this change.

Needs no earlier patch.

Not yet checked against upstream main.

Delete this patch when go.mod requires an upstream release that contains the
change.

